p=base/'README.md';s=p.read_text();s+='\n## Qualified assertion scope\n\n[Scope clarification](scope-clarifications.json) distinguishes the raw output labels from the actual checks. The original strings “full recovered state digest” and “all published window fields” remain unchanged in copied JSON. Recovery compares a **durable semantic-projection digest**: watermark/duplicates, source offsets/maxima, dedup entries, panes, nonfinal results, pending windows and admitted keys. It excludes rebased activity/idle fields, run/limits, late counters, quarantine, outbox and finalized results; it is not byte-for-byte full snapshot equality. The SQL oracle independently checks key/end/count/sum/minimum/maximum/finality and row count, and requires **revision >=1**. It does not independently derive exact revision numbers or their sequence; revisions are not included in its result digest. These qualifications change the explanatory scope, not the passed raw measurements or source identity.\n';p.write_text(s)
p=root/'projects/04-pulsestream/docs/PERFORMANCE.md';s=p.read_text().replace('matched its committed/recovered state digest and independently derived result digest', 'matched its committed/recovered durable semantic-projection digest and independently derived aggregate result digest');anchor='Maximum observed queue occupancy was7batches against capacity8.';s=s.replace(anchor,anchor+'\n\nThe recovery digest covers watermark/duplicates, source offsets and maximum timestamps, dedup entries, panes, nonfinal results, pending windows and admitted keys. It excludes partition activity/idle fields intentionally rebased on restart, run identity/limits, late counters, quarantine, outbox and finalized results. It is a semantic projection, not byte-for-byte full snapshot equality. Separately, the SQL oracle checks row count, tenant/sensor/window keys, end, count/sum/minimum/maximum and finality, and requires a positive revision (`revision >=1`). It does not independently derive exact revision values or their sequence; revision is not part of its aggregate result digest. Raw labels claiming “full recovered state digest” and “all published window fields” remain preserved with [this explicit qualification](../evidence/reference-20261018-quiet12/scope-clarifications.json).');p.write_text(s)
p=root/'projects/04-pulsestream/docs/STATUS.md';s=p.read_text().replace('including independent recovery/output digests.', 'including semantic-projection recovery equality and independent aggregate/key/end/finality SQL checks with positive revisions; exact revision sequences are not derived.');s=s.replace('and full committed/recovered digest.', 'and committed/recovered semantic-projection digest.');s+='\n## Qualified measured assertion scope\n\nThe unchanged raw workload labels overstate two assertion boundaries. Recovery equality uses a **durable semantic-projection digest**, not every committed field or serialized snapshot bytes. It includes watermark/duplicates, offsets/maxima, dedup, panes, nonfinal results, pending windows and admitted keys; it omits rebased activity/idle fields, run/limits, late counters, quarantine, outbox and finalized results. The independent SQL oracle checks row count and aggregate/key/end/finality fields and requires revision>=1; it does not derive exact revision values or their sequence. [The scope annotation](../evidence/reference-20261018-quiet12/scope-clarifications.json) records exact inclusions/exclusions and preserves all original source/raw/copiedJSON bytes. The three-round measurement/data PASS remains valid within these limits.\n';p.write_text(s)
p=root/'projects/04-pulsestream/docs/CASE_STUDY.md';s=p.read_text();s+='\nThe full-workload recovery proof compares a durable semantic projection, excluding restart-rebased activity/idle fields and other fields listed in the evidence scope annotation; it is not byte-for-byte whole-state equality. Its independent SQL oracle proves aggregate/key/end/finality values and a positive revision, without deriving the exact revision sequence. The raw broad labels are preserved and qualified in PERFORMANCE.\n';p.write_text(s)
p=root/'projects/04-pulsestream/docs/REVIEW.md';s=p.read_text().replace('exact three-round counts/digests, throughput/CPU arithmetic', 'exact three-round counts, semantic-projection recovery equality and independent SQL aggregate/key/end/finality digests with positive revisions, throughput/CPU arithmetic');s+='\nA03\'s independent quiet12 numerical/lineage review identified two explanatory scope qualifications. `Workload.stateDigest` verifies only its durable semantic projection, with rebased activity/idle and the other explicitly listed fields excluded. The full SQL workload oracle independently checks aggregate/key/end/finality and row count, requiring revision>=1 but not deriving exact revision values or sequence. Current docs and a separate `scope-clarifications.json` now state those boundaries while preserving every original raw/source/copiedJSON byte and the prior19file seal. Wording closure is requested on the qualified packet; no final release approval is implied.\n';p.write_text(s)
